om/users/jlovejoy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-08-28T03:14:28Z","updated_at":"2023-08-28T03:14:28Z","body":"A key aspect of the SPDX License List inclusion principle https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/blob/main/DOCS/license-inclusion-principles.md is substantial use of the license. This is because the overall goal of SPDX is to provide a language for communicating information about software, which presumes it is used in the software supply chain. \r\n\r\nNote in the https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/blob/main/DOCS/request-new-license.md page, it also reiterates this. \r\n\r\nSo, if this is a one-off license for your own project, it doesn't meet that criteria.\r\n\r\nI appreciate you are super excited (although I'm not sure why this is exciting ;)\r\nTaking a step back - why write a new license instead of using an existing one? While this is more of a curious question, it does relate to the overall goal of the open source (license) community to try to avoid license proliferation.  ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1694940597/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1695989607","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2095#issuecomment-1695989607","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2095","id":1695989607,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85lFr9n","user":{"login":"solomonshalom","id":71135230,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxMTM1MjMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71135230?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/solomonshalom","html_url":"https://github.com/solomonshalom","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solomonshalom/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solomonshalom/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solomonshalom/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solomonshalom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solomonshalom/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solomonshalom/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solomonshalom/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solomonshalom/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solomonshalom/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-08-28T16:28:14Z","updated_at":"2023-08-28T16:28:14Z","body":"Hi! @jlovejoy \r\n\r\nHmm, I see but if it does have substantial use, it would be considered, right?\r\n\r\nAlso, Yes! I could have used an existing license but I couldn't find one that had the liberation for modification of it. Note that this license is mainly tailored to those who create products that are OS (like me :D)\r\n\r\nP.S. Super excited because it just seemed cool to publish a license 😅 Though, really appreciate you taking your time and checking my license! ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1695989607/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1709419538","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2095#issuecomment-1709419538","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2095","id":1709419538,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85l46wS","user":{"login":"jlovejoy","id":5048659,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNDg2NTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5048659?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy","html_url":"https://github.com/jlovejoy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-09-07T03:23:20Z","updated_at":"2023-09-07T03:23:20Z","body":" \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n> Hmm, I see but if it does have substantial use, it would be considered, right?\r\n\r\nthen it could be re-submitted and re-considered, yes.\r\n\r\n> Also, Yes! I could have used an existing license but I couldn't find one that had the liberation for modification of it. Note that this license is mainly tailored to those who create products that are OS (like me :D)\r\n\r\nYou might have a look at the Open Source Definition as held by the Open Source Initiative and which is considered to be the definitive definition of an open source license. Your license would not meet that definition due to the restrictions on commercial use. \r\n\r\nYou also might consider that the last bit may be a bit muddy as to how copyright law works and other similar rights in various jurisdictions. \r\n\r\n> P.S. Super excited because it just seemed cool to publish a license 😅 Though, really appreciate you taking your time and checking my license!\r\n\r\nyour welcome!\r\n\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1709419538/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1709658057","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2095#issuecomment-1709658057","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2095","id":1709658057,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85l50_J","user":{"login":"solomonshalom","id":71135230,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxMTM1MjMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71135230?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/solomonshalom","html_url":"https://github.com/solomonshalom","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solomonshalom/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solomonshalom/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solomonshalom/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solomonshalom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solomonshalom/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solomonshalom/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solomonshalom/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solomonshalom/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solomonshalom/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-09-07T07:57:31Z","updated_at":"2023-09-07T07:57:31Z","body":"> > Hmm, I see but if it does have substantial use, it would be considered, right?\r\n> \r\n> then it could be re-submitted and re-considered, yes.\r\n> \r\n> > Also, Yes! I could have used an existing license but I couldn't find one that had the liberation for modification of it. Note that this license is mainly tailored to those who create products that are OS (like me :D)\r\n> \r\n> You might have a look at the Open Source Definition as held by the Open Source Initiative and which is considered to be the definitive definition of an open source license. Your license would not meet that definition due to the restrictions on commercial use.\r\n> \r\n> You also might consider that the last bit may be a bit muddy as to how copyright law works and other similar rights in various jurisdictions.\r\n> \r\n> > P.S. Super excited because it just seemed cool to publish a license 😅 Though, really appreciate you taking your time and checking my license!\r\n> \r\n> your welcome!\r\n\r\n1. I see! Wonderful (I shall come again <3)\r\n\r\n2. Hmm, I understand and although it has a basis on commercial-restriction, the license also gives anybody holding the license the liberty to modify the license as per their requirements. It was initially created to support open-source projects that have a business side to them and to protect their service / product. \r\n\r\nThank you for taking your time! It does mean a lot :D","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1709658057/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1711030860","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2095#issuecomment-1711030860","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2095","id":1711030860,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85l_EJM","user":{"login":"jlovejoy","id":5048659,"node_id":"MDQ